  "claims": [],
  "shared_decisions": [
    {
      "id": "D1",
      "phase": "B2",
      "decision": "R7 dropped: phases are designed from the audits; unobserved behaviour is marked [assumed]",
      "affects": [
        "B2",
        "B4",
        "B5",
        "B6",
        "B11"
      ],
      "source": "spec 2026-10-02 PO-2"
    },
    {
      "id": "D2",
      "phase": "B8",
      "decision": "No academy-supplied script or raw HTML executes on an academy host: the public site shares its origin with /app/ and /api/ and the CSRF cookie is script-readable. Third-party integrations are validated IDs rendered from fixed templates; user-uploaded HTML/SVG is never served inline from the academy origin.",
      "affects": [
        "B8",
        "B9",
        "B10"
      ],
      "source": "spec 2026-10-03-b8a A-7"
    },
    {
      "id": "D3",
      "phase": "B3",
      "decision": "Expenses live in new app etqan.finance. Other apps post expenses only via finance.services.post_expense(source, source_id, title, type, amount_minor, currency, spent_on, notes='') — idempotent per (source, source_id) — and withdraw_expense(source, source_id); posted expenses are read-only in the API. B4 posts paid payslips with source 'payroll.payslip', type 'salaries' (PAY-013).",
      "affects": [
        "B4"
      ],
      "source": "spec 2026-10-03-b3a A-8; audit PAY-013"
    },
    {
      "id": "D4",
      "phase": "B3",
      "decision": "Online payments live in new app etqan.gateways (Stripe + PayPal, each academy's own merchant keys, Fernet-encrypted under env ETQAN_SECRETS_KEY). Other apps take online money only via gateways.services.start_checkout(purpose, ...) with a per-purpose completion handler registered by the owning app; only the provider webhook (/api/v1/gateways/webhooks/<provider>/) marks a checkout paid. Exact signature fixed by B3b's spec.",
      "affects": [
        "B7",
        "B11"
      ],
      "source": "spec 2026-10-03-b3 B3-6/B3-7"
    },
    {
      "id": "D5",
      "phase": "B3",
      "decision": "Revenue = completed payment records only (BR-47); donations are not revenue; net profit = revenue - expenses per currency per academy month (BR-48); never summed across currencies.",
      "affects": [
        "B4",
        "B7"
      ],
      "source": "P1 BR-47/48; spec 2026-10-03-b3 B3-5"
    },
    {
      "id": "D6",
      "phase": "B2",
      "decision": "Group classes are one Session row per roster student (same time, linked by the group), each with its own attendance and consumption; how a teacher is paid for a group class is B4's",
      "affects": [
        "B4",
        "B5",
        "B6",
        "B11"
      ],
      "source": "spec docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-03-b2-scheduling-depth-design.md B2-2"
    },
    {
      "id": "D7",
      "phase": "B2",
      "decision": "Subscription keeps its meaning (one student, course, teacher, package). Multi-course, family and group subscriptions are a bundle grouping several Subscriptions; billing, payroll and notifications keep reading single subscriptions",
      "affects": [
        "B3",
        "B4",
        "B5",
        "B6",
        "B11"
      ],
      "source": "spec docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-03-b2-scheduling-depth-design.md B2-3"
    },
    {
      "id": "D8",
      "phase": "B2",
      "decision": "Session.kind regular|compensation|extra|trial; only regular and compensation (not compensated) consume the package; status gains at_disposal (never consumes; today's payroll rule does not pay it)",
      "affects": [
        "B4",
        "B5",
        "B6",
        "B11"
      ],
      "source": "spec docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-03-b2-scheduling-depth-design.md B2-4, B2-6"
    },
    {
      "id": "D9",
      "phase": "B2",
      "decision": "Session.pays_teacher (default true): scheduling.payroll_sessions leaves out sessions with it off; a hand-added session in an issued month is paid as a later adjustment (P7-4)",
      "affects": [
        "B4"
      ],
      "source": "spec docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-03-b2-scheduling-depth-design.md B2-5; B2a A-15"
    },
    {
      "id": "D10",
      "phase": "B2",
      "decision": "SUB-006 payment type (prepaid/postpaid) and subscription system (normal/monthly) are B3's payment metadata, not B2's",
      "affects": [
        "B3"
      ],
      "source": "spec docs/superpowers/specs/2026-10-03-b2-scheduling-depth-design.md §3"
    },
    {
      "id": "D11",
      "phase": "B9",
      "decision": "Spanish arrives in B9d (dashboard + emails). Other phases add en and ar strings only; a missing es string falls back to English per key; the ar/en key-equality test is unchanged; the public site stays ar/en in B9.",
      "affects": [
        "B2",
        "B3",
        "B4",
        "B5",
        "B6",
        "B7",
        "B8",
        "B10",
        "B11"
      ],
      "source": "spec 2026-10-03-platform-extras B9-6"
    },
    {
      "id": "D12",
      "phase": "B9",
      "decision": "etqan.platform.uploads (B9a) offers shared upload checks: extension + content signature table, size cap, Pillow re-encode of PNG/JPEG/WEBP, tenant_upload_path. Available for reuse; no phase is required to switch to it. Private (non-public) files use STORAGES['private'] (DJANGO_S3_PRIVATE_BUCKET in production).",
      "affects": [
        "B6",
        "B7",
        "B8"
      ],
      "source": "spec 2026-10-03-platform-extras A-7, A-10"
    },
    {
      "id": "D13",
      "phase": "B3",
      "decision": "Supersedes D4's interface text: other apps take online money via gateways.services.start_checkout(purpose, reference_id, provider, *, user, params=None) -> StartedCheckout{id, redirect_url, amount_minor, fee_minor, currency}, after register_purpose(name, *, prepare(reference_id, user, params) -> Prepared(amount_minor, currency, description, add_fee), complete(CompletedCheckout) -> Applied(ok, reason)) in AppConfig.ready(). A verified provider event (or, for PayPal from B3c, a verified server-side capture response) completes a checkout from any state but completed; money that cannot be applied stays as applied=false 'needs attention'. Stripe in B3b, PayPal in B3c.",
      "affects": [
        "B7",
        "B11"
      ],
      "source": "spec 2026-10-03-b3b B-1, B-4, §4.2-4.3"
    },
    {
      "id": "D14",
      "phase": "B2",
      "decision": "Archived subscriptions and sessions (B2d) are the same rows with archived_at set, hidden only from the office's default scheduling lists and Today board. Other apps never filter on archived_at: invoices, payroll, consumption, notifications and reports keep counting archived rows (BR-46 'table + archive').",
      "affects": [
        "B3",
        "B4",
        "B5",
        "B11"
      ],
      "source": "spec 2026-10-03-b2d-archives D-2 (draft, B2d branch); P1 BR-46"
    },
    {
      "id": "D15",
      "phase": "B2",
      "decision": "Until B4 decides group pay, today's payroll rule pays a group class once per student row (D6), since payroll_sessions is unchanged. B2f also adds an optional member_id to etqan.platform ConflictError/ValidationError (additive; the exception handler adds it to the body when set).",
      "affects": [
        "B4",
        "B11"
      ],
      "source": "spec 2026-10-03-b2f-bundles-groups §10, §4.6 (draft, B2f branch)"
    },
    {
      "id": "D16",
      "phase": "B3",
      "decision": "Refines D5: revenue = amount_minor + fee_minor of completed billing payments, with or without an invoice, grouped by Payment.currency. Payment.invoice becomes nullable and every Payment carries its own currency (B3g).",
      "affects": [
        "B4",
        "B7"
      ],
      "source": "spec 2026-10-03-b3g G-1, G-4"
    },
    {
      "id": "D17",
      "phase": "B3",
      "decision": "Extends D13: PayPal completes via server-side capture POST /api/v1/gateways/checkouts/<uuid>/capture/ (re-checks still-payable under a short lock; else cancels, captures nothing); PayPal refunds/reversals only set attention. Checkouts of purposes payment_link (billing) and donation_link (finance) are readable/capturable/cancellable/simulatable by anyone holding the UUID (decided by purpose; B7 registers its own purposes for anonymous access). /app/pay/return and /app/pay/simulate/$id are public routes. gateways never imports a selling app; other apps reach gateways only through gateways.services (import contract).",
      "affects": [
        "B7",
        "B11"
      ],
      "source": "spec 2026-10-03-b3c C-7/C-8/C-11/C-13; b3g G-15, G-22"
    },
    {
      "id": "D18",
      "phase": "B3",
      "decision": "Confirms D10: SUB-006 payment type/subscription system live in billing.SubscriptionTerms keyed by subscription id; B2 adds no fields or hooks; a renewal starts from defaults; office-only metadata nothing reads.",
      "affects": [
        "B2"
      ],
      "source": "spec 2026-10-03-b3g G-18, G-19; ledger D10"
    }
  ],
